&Q000762 = The debate between Winter and Summer
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.5.3.3
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.5.3.3&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. [an-ne₂ nam]-nir-ra saŋ mi-ni-in-il₂ ud dug₃ am₃-mi-e₃
#tr.en: @wDN{An} lifted his head in pride and brought forth a good day.
#lem: An[1]DN; namnir[supremacy]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; ud[sun]; dug[good]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 29; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 30; OB catalogue from Urim (U2), 0.2.04, line 22; OB catalogue from Nibru (N4), 0.2.08, Seg. D, line 2

2. [...]-ke₄ ŋiš-hur ba-an-sig₁₀ uŋ₃-e daŋal bi₂-in-tag
#tr.en: He laid plans for …… and spread the population wide.
#lem: X; ŋešhur[plan]; sig[put into]; uŋ[people]; daŋal[wide]; tag[touch]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. {[d]}[en]-lil₂#-le ki-a gud gal-gin₇ ŋiri₃-ni nam-mi-in-gub
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} set his foot upon the earth like a great bull.
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; ki[place]; gud[bull]; gal[big]; ŋiri[foot]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. ud dug₃ nam-he₂-a buluŋ₃-e-de₃
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, the king of all lands,
#lem: ud[sun]; dug[good]; namhe[abundance]; buluŋ[grow]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. ŋi₆ X X giri₁₇-zal-e pa e₃ ak-de₃
#tr.en: set his mind to increasing the good day of abundance,
#lem: ŋi[night]; X; X; kirizal[joy]; pa[branch]; e[leave]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. gu mu₂-mu₂-de₃ še daŋal-e-de₃
#tr.en: to making the …… night resplendent in celebration,
#lem: gu[cord]; mu[grow]; še[barley]; daŋal[wide]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. a-eštub{ku₆} kar-ra gen₆-ne₂-de₃
#tr.en: to making flax grow, to making barley proliferate,
#lem: aʾeštub[early flooding]; kar[harbor]; gin[confirm]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. [...] X-e nam-he₂-a ud sud₄-su₁₃-ru-de₃
#tr.en: to guaranteeing the spring floods at the quay,
#lem: X; X; namhe[abundance]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. e₂-me-eš an-na niŋ₂-keše₂ ak-de₃
#tr.en: to making …… lengthen (?) their days in abundance,
#lem: emeš[summer]; an[sky]; niŋkešed[band]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. en-te-en a he₂-ŋal₂-la kar-ra gen₆-ne₂-de₃
#tr.en: to making Summer close the sluices of heaven,
#lem: enten[winter]; a[water]; heŋal[plenty]; kar[harbor]; gin[confirm]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. {d}en-lil₂ lugal kur-kur-ra-ke₄ ŋeštug₂-ga-ni na-an-gub
#tr.en: and to making Winter guarantee plentiful water at the quay.
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; lugal[king]; kur[mountain(s)]; ŋeštug[ear]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. hur-saŋ gal-gal-la ŋiš₃ bi₂-in-dug₄ kur-re ha-la ba-an-šum₂
#tr.en: He copulated with the great hills, he gave the mountain its share.
#lem: hursaŋ[mountain]; gal[big]; ŋeš[penis]; dug[speak]; kur[mountain(s)]; hala[inheritance share]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. e₂-me-eš en-te-en he₂-ŋal₂ zi kalam-ma šag₄-ga mu-ni-in-ri
#tr.en: He filled its womb with Summer and Winter, the plenitude and life of the Land.
#lem: emeš[summer]; enten[winter]; heŋal[plenty]; zi[life]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; šag[heart]; ri[impose]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. {d}en-lil₂-le ki ŋiš₃ dug₄-ga-ni am-gin₇ mur im-ša₄
#tr.en: As @wDN{Enlil} copulated with the earth, there was a roar like a bull's.
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; ki[place]; ŋeš[penis]; dug[speak]; am[wild bull]; mur[noise]; ša[cvve]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. hur-saŋ-e ud ki-bi-še₃ nam-zal ŋi₆ haš₄ nam-mi-ib-dug₄
#tr.en: The hill spent the day at that place and at night she opened her loins.
#lem: hursaŋ[mountain]; ud[sun]; ki[place]; zal[pass time]; ŋi[night]; haš[thigh]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. e₂-me-eš en-te-en i₃-he-nun-na-gin₇ šu nam-ta-ab-us₂
#tr.en: She bore Summer and Winter as smoothly as fine oil.
#lem: emeš[summer]; enten[winter]; ihenunak[precious oil]; šu[hand]; us[accompany]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. am gal-gin₇ temen-na hur-saŋ-ŋa₂-ka u₂ sikil mu-un-gu₇-e
#tr.en: He fed them pure plants on the terraces of the hills like great bulls.
#lem: am[wild bull]; gal[big]; temen[foundation]; hursaŋ[mountain]; u[plant(s)]; sikil[purify]; gu[eat]
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. šag₄-tum₂-šag₄-tum₂ hur-saŋ-ŋa₂-ka gu₂ mu-un-peš-peš-e
#tr.en: He nourished them in the pastures of the hills.
#lem: šagtum[pasture land]; hursaŋ[mountain]; gu[neck]; peš[thick]
#etcsl: line-id=18

